# ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. Everything is ignored by default and only source
# is re-included, so a new artifact directory can never be committed by
# accident. This matters here: profiles/ holds nsys reports (binary, and nsys
# captures the process environment), coredumps/ holds raw process memory, and
# logs/ holds full command lines -- any of which can carry an HF_TOKEN or
# similar. Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so the negations
# below only ever re-include files at the repo root.
*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!upstream_writeup_*.md
!*.py
!*.sh
!*.cu
!*.cpp

# Belt and braces: named explicitly so they stay out even if the rules above
# are ever loosened to allow subdirectories.
.venv/
logs/
profiles/
dumps/
coredumps/
.vllm_cache/
__pycache__/
.claude/
*.nsys-rep
*.sqlite
*.json
*.log
*.pt
*.safetensors

# Local only -- deliberately NOT published. Hardware bring-up diagnostics from
# the CMP 170HX 64 GB unlock / Xid 31 investigation, and the MiniMax-M2.7
# setup that shares this box. Neither is part of serving GLM-5.2.
alloc_pattern_test.py
ce_coverage_test.py
gpu_stress.py
hbm_soak.py
mmap_load_test.py
real_alloc_test.py
nccl_pp_test.py
bench.py
copy_model.sh
serve_minimax.sh
